=== TITLE: USG Abdomen & Pelvis (Female) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NO SIGNIFICANT SONOLOGICAL ABNORMALITY DETECTED IN ABDOMEN AND PELVIS.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF WHOLE ABDOMEN & PELVIS (FEMALE)

FINDINGS:
- LIVER: Normal in size (13.6 cm), contour, and parenchymal echotexture. No focal lesion, cyst, or intrahepatic biliary radicle dilatation (IHBRD) seen. Portal vein is normal in caliber.
- GALL BLADDER: Well-distended with clear lumen. Wall thickness is normal (2.2 mm). No calculus or mass lesion.
- COMMON BILE DUCT (CBD): Normal in caliber, measuring 3.5 mm.
- PANCREAS: Visualized portions are normal in size and echotexture. Main pancreatic duct (MPD) is not dilated.
- SPLEEN: Normal in size (9.6 cm) with homogeneous echotexture. Splenic vein is normal.
- KIDNEYS:
  * Right Kidney: Measures 10.2 cm. Cortical thickness 14 mm. Normal corticomedullary differentiation. No calculus, hydronephrosis, or focal mass.
  * Left Kidney: Measures 10.5 cm. Cortical thickness 14.5 mm. Normal corticomedullary differentiation. No calculus, hydronephrosis, or focal mass.
- URINARY BLADDER: Well-distended with thin, smooth walls. Lumen is clear. No calculus, mass, or diverticulum.
- UTERUS: Anteverted, measures normal in size (7.8 x 4.2 x 3.6 cm). Myometrial echotexture is homogeneous. Endometrial thickness (ET) is 6.8 mm, centrally located.
- OVARIES: Both ovaries are normal in size, shape, and stroma. No adnexal cyst or mass lesion visualized.
- PERITONEAL CAVITY: No free fluid, ascites, or significant retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.